Usage: ruralz node drain [FLAGS]

Drain the local ruralzd.

Sends SIGTERM to the ruralzd that holds the lock on the data directory, as a
process manager does, once holder.json, the PID namespace, the process start
time and /proc/locks confirm that process, then waits until it exits.

Flags:
  --data-dir PATH     Data directory of the local ruralzd (default $RURALZ_DATA_DIR, else /var/lib/ruralz)
  --help              Print this help
  --output text|json  Output format (text or json, default text)
  --timeout DURATION  How long to await the exit after the signal (default 5m)
